            <p>A book-length history of the district of Nosara, combining archival research (national archive, judicial records, vital statistics) with oral history interviews of the founding criollo families and the post-1968 settlement period. First book-length community history of the district.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="pub-item">
          <div class="pub-meta">
            <h3>Territorial Fiscal Balance - methodology replication <span class="pub-badge pub-badge-done">Delivered</span></h3>
            <div class="pub-source">Methodology - 2026 - JP Asesores</div>
            <p>Documenting and packaging the Territorial Fiscal Balance methodology so it can be replicated by other districts and municipalities in Costa Rica and Central America. Open methodology, auditable sources, transferable workflow.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="pub-item">
          <div class="pub-meta">
            <h3>Digital Twins, Heat Maps and Policy for the Future <span class="pub-badge pub-badge-done">Delivered</span></h3>
            <div class="pub-source">R&amp;D - 2026 - JP Asesores / ADC</div>
            <p>Real-time territorial digital twins, heat maps and policy simulation tools to anticipate and design futures for districts and municipalities. First deployment delivered: the <a href="https://desarrollocomunitario.org/gemelodigital" target="_blank">Nosara 3D Digital Twin</a>.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="pub-item">
          <div class="pub-meta">
            <h3>Agentic, Internet-AI Native Institutions <span class="pub-badge pub-badge-done">Delivered</span></h3>
            <div class="pub-source">Applied research - 2026 - JP Asesores</div>
            <p>Designing institutions from scratch for the era of agentic AI and an internet-native public: governance models that assume continuous data flow, autonomous agents and distributed decision-making. Applied to local governments, community organizations and impact-driven ventures.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="pub-item">
          <div class="pub-meta">
            <h3>Predictive models for territorial decisions <span class="pub-badge pub-badge-done">Delivered</span></h3>
            <div class="pub-source">Methodology - 2026 - JP Asesores</div>
            <p>A working methodology for building auditable predictive models that municipalities and community organizations can actually use. A 6-check protocol (posterior predictive check, linearity, homoscedasticity, influential points, VIF, normality) and a simple-to-complex catalog (regression / Lasso / tree → random forest / boosting → Bayesian hierarchical). Interpretability as a governance requirement, not a nice-to-have.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="pub-item">
          <div class="pub-meta">
            <h3>Governance models, cycle-breaking, resilience and community-institutional restoration <span class="pub-badge pub-badge-done">Delivered</span></h3>
            <div class="pub-source">Applied research - 2026 - JP Asesores</div>
            <p>Designing governance models that recognize three distinct institutional functions: Architect (verifiable data, protocol of integrity), Oracle (interface that translates evidence into agency), and Cycle-breaker (questioning rules with information, organization and legitimacy). Applied to community-institutional restoration: how to break extractive feedback loops without breaking the institutions themselves.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

